DECISION — 2027/EU-AIA-0215 (adopted 2027-07-09; applies from 2027-12-02)

The AI Office adopts the High-Risk Readiness Package, released ahead of the deferred high-risk date of 2027-12-02.

Contents:
· Model documentation template v3.0 — now aligned with the incident taxonomy circulated for the 2027-09-14 technical round;
· Conformity-assessment self-check for Annex III deployers, in all EU languages;
· Serious-incident reporting channel, live and tested; median acknowledgement 4 business days;
· A public register of Article 55 document requests, including 2027/EU-AIA-0208 (GPT-6.1 Astra), with responses due 2027-08-12.

Why now: the 2026-05-07 provisional deal moved the high-risk obligations to 2027-12-02. It did not move the date on which firms should start preparing. Support tools in place before the rule applies is the difference between compliance and a cliff edge.

Nothing in this package creates new obligations. It exists so that the obligations arriving in December are already legible.
